WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.602
Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.870
can be taken into custody

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.139
in 123 different countries.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.974
Now that the International Criminal Court

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.176
has issued a warrant for his arrest

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.579
He and the Russian official in this photo

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.947
are accused of scheming

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.082
to deport thousands of Ukrainian children

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.117
to Russia.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.752
White House national security aide John

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.520
Kirby says it's critical

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.288
that all evidence against Putin

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.957
be preserved.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:24.457
Well, things

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.625
first, we're going to stay committed

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.893
to helping Ukraine

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.695
as they document and analyze

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.629
and preserve

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.264
the kinds of evidence of the war

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.932
crimes, the atrocities, the crimes

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.967
against humanity

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:34.901
that have occurred inside

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.303
Ukraine at the hands of Russian forces.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.571
And number two,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.073
that we are not going to back off

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:40.840
our belief

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.742
that accountability for these war crimes

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.877
has got to be had,

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.145
however long that takes

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.582
one place, Putin won't be arrested.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.017
Crimea, he's

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:51.885
in the annexed region

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:52.786
today for the nine year

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:55.255
anniversary of Russia's takeover.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.389
CNN national security

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.091
analyst Steve Hall joins us now.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:58.558
He's also

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.026
the former CIA chief

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:02.295
of Russian operations.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.329
Steve,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.031
what do you what do you make of this?

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.465
I mean, could

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.567
he ever actually be arrested,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:11.337
it seems at this point, improbable

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.573
You know, it is improbable right now.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.141
So this action has

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.743
a lot of different ramifications.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.277
I think first

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:17.510
it does

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.312
send a strong message

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:22.215
to Putin and to the Russians in general.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:22.549
You know,

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.817
Russians on the streets, senior

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.684
Russian leadership, and,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.319
of course, Putin himself,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.921
that they're increased.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.522
They're increasingly isolated

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.191
from from basically

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.193
the entire international community.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:33.860
And although,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.094
you know,

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.595
I will say it's unlikely

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.796
that he'll be arrested.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:37.363
But remember,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.731
we also said it was unlikely

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.767
that we'd get guys like Milosevic

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.203
You know, from from the Serbian

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.438
Ratko Mladic, his military commander.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.906
And yet they both ended up in The Hague

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:47.774
eventually.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.809
It took time, but it did happen.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.910
So I'm sure that Putin

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.878
is remembering

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:52.412
those things

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:52.946
and remembering

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.214
that this is not a temporary thing

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.982
that goes away after a year or two.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.250
It stays with you forever.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.084
And it'll be interesting

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.986
to see how that impacts upon him.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.155
If at all in his decision making.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.323
It's a long game.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.157
And of course, the US

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.226
is not an ICC signatory,

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.460
and neither is Russia.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.628
Does that have any effect

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.530
on diplomatic relations?

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.898
Between Washington and Moscow?

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.901
I really don't think it does.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.435
I mean,

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.236
this is certainly,

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.204
you know, a bad day for Vladimir Putin

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.906
or yesterday was and for Russia.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.509
And so that's not going to increase

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.811
the, you know, any sort of activity

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.912
or negotiations

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.180
either with the United States

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.749
or any of our Western allies or Ukraine

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:30.316
for that matter.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.784
But just because the United States

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.619
is not a signatory

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.487
to this particular treaty

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.789
doesn't mean that it can't assist

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.991
in obtaining information,

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.625
which is I think

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.626
what what

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:40.160
Admiral Kirby

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:40.960
was talking about there,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.662
the importance of preserving

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.297
any information, any data,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.865
any proof or evidence

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:46.866
that Putin was involved

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:47.967
in what he's been accused of,

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.170
and in that anybody in in the world

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.171
can help with that

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.205
to include the United States.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.773
You don't have to be a signatory

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.775
to help with the process.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.709
Of course, next week,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:57.877
Putin is scheduled to meet

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.411
with the Chinese

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.679
president, Xi Jinping,

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.681
to discuss the war in Ukraine.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.849
Do you think this warrant

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.685
will have any effect on Chinese Russian

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.686
relations?

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:09.656
Probably not

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.291
at the level that we can see it,

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.091
but I can tell you

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.526
that I think one of the impacts

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.161
that this will have

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.162
is condemnation

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.964
and this

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.265
arrest warrant for Putin is going to

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:19.966
have is

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.100
if you're a world leader

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.835
and you want to be taken seriously,

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.370
do you want to be on camera

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.072
publicly meeting with somebody

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.707
that has been officially designated

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.209
as a war criminal

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.009
in that that is

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.044
I think, going to be in the back

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.412
of a lot of people's minds,

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.680
especially if they're contemplating

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.781
meeting with Russia.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:35.481
Now, granted

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.015
the countries

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:36.449
that Russia

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:36.683
and that

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.684
Putin usually meet with

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.919
are usually not friendly to the West,

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.454
but China is very concerned

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.455
over the long run

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:42.789
as to

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:43.623
what its role is

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:44.490
going to be in the future.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.326
It wants to be a significant

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:47.560
global superpower

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.028
and it wants to dominate things

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.230
20, five, 30 years from now.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.397
And so if somebody's

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.899
got those ideas about

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.866
where their country is going to go,

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.235
is it really in their best interest

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:57.270
to meet with a designated war criminal?

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.404
We'll see.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:03:59.472
We'll see.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.440
And Putin is also,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.140
of course,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.975
scheduled to attend

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.110
a summit in South Africa later this year.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.512
They are a signatory to the ICC

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.981
and each chance

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.083
he may be asked to attend that remotely.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.050
Or do you think he'll attend to

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.784
they could bring him in?

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:13.853
That's very interesting.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.622
I mean, if I were the South Africans,

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:16.222
you know, I would

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.056
I would have to treat this

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.625
very very carefully.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.026
They're trying to walk sort of,

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.361
you know, sort of a middle ground.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.962
They've been supportive on Russia

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:23.763
on certain things.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.297
But remember,

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.164
the South Africans

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:25.999
a number of years ago

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.301
failed to capture an individual

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.936
who was designated

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.770
the same way that Putin

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.571
has been designated

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:32.872
an arrest warrant out for him

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.573
in the South.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.041
Africans received

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:35.975
considerable criticism

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.210
for not picking up that person.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.278
So this

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:39.078
you know, this is, again,

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.947
something that internationally, countries

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:41.547
and governments

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:41.948
are going to have

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.116
to take into consideration

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.018
before they have contact

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:47.587
or have warm ties with Russia.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.655
Steve, all, thank you.

